Subject: [PATCH] abseil: treat WASIX as a platform with mmap()

Abseil 20250814.1 only lists Emscripten among WebAssembly targets that have
mmap(); the 20230802.1 release bundled with MySQL 8.4 accepted any __wasm__
target. Without ABSL_HAVE_MMAP, ABSL_LOW_LEVEL_ALLOC_MISSING is defined and
low_level_alloc.cc, create_thread_identity.cc and per_thread_sem.cc compile
to nothing, so absl::Mutex and the stack tracer no longer link (protoc fails
with undefined CreateThreadIdentity, PerThreadSem and LowLevelAlloc symbols).

WASIX provides mmap() through wasi-libc's emulation, and MySQL 8.4's WASIX
build has been using Abseil's LowLevelAlloc on top of it, so add __wasi__ to
the list.

diff --git a/extra/abseil/abseil-cpp-20250814.1/absl/base/config.h b/extra/abseil/abseil-cpp-20250814.1/absl/base/config.h
index b2557b89..d9e76d10 100644
--- a/extra/abseil/abseil-cpp-20250814.1/absl/base/config.h
+++ b/extra/abseil/abseil-cpp-20250814.1/absl/base/config.h
@@ -372,6 +372,8 @@ static_assert(ABSL_INTERNAL_INLINE_NAMESPACE_STR[0] != 'h' ||
 //
 // Checks whether the platform has an mmap(2) implementation as defined in
 // POSIX.1-2001.
+// WASIX provides mmap() through wasi-libc's emulation; without it
+// LowLevelAlloc, and with it Mutex, would not be available.
 #ifdef ABSL_HAVE_MMAP
 #error ABSL_HAVE_MMAP cannot be directly set
 #elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) ||    \
@@ -379,7 +381,8 @@ static_assert(ABSL_INTERNAL_INLINE_NAMESPACE_STR[0] != 'h' ||
     defined(__asmjs__) || defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__Fuchsia__) || \
     defined(__sun) || defined(__myriad2__) || defined(__HAIKU__) ||          \
     defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__QNX__) ||       \
-    defined(__VXWORKS__) || defined(__hexagon__) || defined(__XTENSA__)
+    defined(__VXWORKS__) || defined(__hexagon__) || defined(__XTENSA__) ||   \
+    defined(__wasi__)
 #define ABSL_HAVE_MMAP 1
 #endif
 
